SUMMARY:High Park Hikeathon: A Fundraiser For Nature Connection
DESCRIPTION:FrogWatch and Turtle Tally in High Park with the 62nd Pathfinders of Toronto				\n				\n				\n				\n									Monday\, June 1\, 2026\, 6:30-8PM 								\n				\n					\n		\n				\n			\n							\n		\n					\n		\n				\n						\n					\n			\n						\n				\n									NOTE: Pre-registration is required for all our events\, hikes and workshops. We do this to ensure we don’t exceed our capacity for indoor events or the maximum limits for group sizes on High Park’s ecologically sensitive trails. Please register on our website before coming to High Park. We cannot guarantee availability of walk-in spots. If an event is at capacity\, please put yourself on our waitlist. We will notify waitlisted participants if we open up new spots or sessions for our events. Please contact us if you have any questions. 								\n				\n				\n				\n					FrogWatch and Turtle Tally in High Park with the 62nd Pathfinders of Toronto				\n				\n				\n				\n									Head out for an evening of FrogWatch and Turtle Tally in High Park with the 62nd Pathfinders of Toronto and High Park Nature Centre. The Pathfinders will start the evening with a presentation inside the Nature Centre on how to identify the frogs and turtles in High Park. Then\, they’ll guide participants through a hands-on community science experience outside listening for frog calls and collecting real data that scientists use to understand the health of frog populations across Ontario. Along the way\, they’ll share fascinating frog facts\, their contagious love for these wetland wanderers\, and invite participants to take part in conservation research in action. Note: Frogs are wild animals and keep their own schedules so they might not be heard or seen during the event and that’s okay. Recording when frogs and turtles aren’t detected is just as important and helps build a clearer picture of how populations are changing over time. Price: FREEMeeting Location: High Park Forest School\, 375 Colborne Lodge Drive 								\n				\n				\n				\n									\n					\n						\n									Register Now\n					\n					\n				\n								\n				\n					\n		\n					\n		\n				\n						\n					\n			\n						\n				\n																														\n				\n				\n				\n																														\n				\n				\n						\n					\n			\n							\n		\n				\n			\n						\n				\n							\n							\n					\n												\n															\n								\n													\n												Date & Time\n					\n\n					Day: Monday\, June 1\, 2026Time: 6:30-8PM\n				\n							\n					\n												\n															\n								\n													\n												Location\n					\n\n					This event will start at the High Park Forest School building located at 375 Colborne Lodge Drive. A number of changes were made to the travel network within High Park as part of the High Park Movement Strategy that might influence your decision to drive to High Park. In case you’re driving we strongly recommend you to park your car at the public parking lot near Grenadier Cafe. We continue to recommend using the TTC or biking as the best way to get to High Park and the Nature Centre. The Nature Centre is situated just a 5-minute walk from the High Park Subway Station. Please note\, High Park is closed to cars on the weekends. If your event is on a weekend\, you will need to park outside the park and walk in\, or take transit. Visit our How To Get Here page to learn more about planning your trips to High Park. \n				\n							\n					\n												\n															\n								\n													\n												Price\n					\n\n					General Admission: FREE\n				\n							\n					\n												\n															\n								\n													\n												Accessibility\n					\n\n					Hike routes through High Park might include some uneven terrain and mild slopes. The High Park Forest School building is not yet an AODA-compliant facility. We try our best to accommodate accessibility needs on a case-by-case basis. Please reach out to us about any accessibility-related questions you might have. \n				\n							\n					\n												\n															\n								\n													\n												Dogs\, Pets and Service Animals\n					\n\n					Dogs and other pets are not permitted in our programs. However\, certified service animals\, such as registered therapy or guide dogs\, are welcome. \n				\n								\n						\n				\n				\n				\n									\n					\n						\n									Register Now\n					\n					\n				\n								\n				\n					\n		\n				\n			\n							\n		\n					\n		\n					\n		\n					\n		\n				\n					\n			\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n		\n				\n			\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n		\n					\n					\n			\n						\n				\n					Registration Policies 				\n				\n				\n				\n									Please ensure you’ve read and understood our registration policies:								\n				\n				\n				\n							\n							\n											\n													\n										General Cancellation Policy\n									\n								\n											\n													\n										Extreme Weather-Related Cancellation Policy\n									\n								\n											\n													\n										Behaviour Policy\n									\n						\n						\n				\n				\n				\n									\n					\n						\n									Read Our Registration Policies
URL:https://highparknaturecentre.com/event/high-park-hikeathon-2026/
LOCATION:High Park Forest School\, 375 Colborne Lodge Drive\, Toronto\, ON\, M6P 3K8\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Nature Hike,Special Events
